  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One app, two ways to play",
      "items": [
        "The shell opens a room first when the link carries a code or a room session is saved, then a saved local round, otherwise the hub. (src/App.jsx:64–81)",
        "The hub seats the party and offers one phone or a room; the game library lists the games that mode supports and opens the chosen game's screen. Games are one registry entry each. (src/App.jsx:173–198; src/games/index.js:20–38)",
        "Both modes render the same screen per phase, so a phase looks the same on one phone and in a room. (src/modes/screens.js:19–54)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What stays on the phone",
      "items": [
        "Pass-and-play keeps everything in localStorage: the active round, settings, recent words, scores and custom packs, each saved as it changes. A private window just forgets. (src/modes/local/LocalGame.jsx:84–127; src/modes/local/storage.js:22–80)",
        "The pack library saves added and written packs to the same shelf. (src/features/packs/Library.jsx:28–37; src/features/packs/store.js:35–56)",
        "Display and sound are per device, never a game setting; sound is off until turned on. The room client also keeps its session here so a reload rejoins. (src/ui/sound/store.js:1–23; src/modes/online/room.js:23–45)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Word packs and the community shelf",
      "items": [
        "Built-in packs load one language at a time as separate chunks; the room service waits for them before it deals. (src/content/words/builtin/index.js:28–80; server/server.js:290–303)",
        "Anyone can share a pack through the Share-a-pack issue form. A maintainer reads every word, adds it with npm run community, and merges it, so the site only fetches its own files. (.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/share-a-pack.yml:1–32; tools/community.mjs:1–50; src/content/words/community.js:1–36)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Rooms are checked on the server",
      "items": [
        "Actions arrive as POSTs, pass a per-caller rate limit, and are dispatched by the room manager, which enforces host rules before running the shared reducer. (server/server.js:173–263; server/limits.js:78–92; server/rooms.js:273–312)",
        "Each phone receives the public table plus only its own private view over SSE, so the word never reaches the imposter's phone. (src/core/select.js:98–219; server/rooms.js:346–391)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Deployments and recovery",
      "items": [
        "Every push to main builds with BASE_PATH=/The-Long-Table/ and deploys to GitHub Pages; CI runs tests, coverage and the browser sweeps on every push and pull request. Pages cannot host rooms. (.github/workflows/pages.yml:1–49; .github/workflows/ci.yml:13–55)",
        "Rooms need a Node host; render.yaml describes Render with six-character codes. (render.yaml:13–28)",
        "Rooms are saved to .rooms.json through a temporary file and a rename and restored after a restart. The file holds the word in play, so it is ignored by git and written 0600. (server/store.js:42–48, 100–108, 144–175; README.md:108–117)"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
